      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=\\frac{1}{x+1}-3?$",
      "worked_solution": "The given function can be obtained by translating $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ both horizontally and vertically.\n\nWe have two translations:\n\n- the $+1$ in the denominator means a horizontal translation of $1$ unit to the *left*, and\n\n- the $-3$ outside the fraction means a vertical translation of $3$ unit *down*.\n\nSo, the new graph looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242844/assets/b9fd8ac22af99f7bd6f3afb039d58c4d2d790d6f9317de855c7f74fa4e5e2fd9.png)",
